    "RETROACTIVE STORY CRITIQUE \u2014 E182 S1\n\nThe story executor for E182 S1 (commit 0b989cb2 on the main branch) skipped\nthe codex critique step before committing. This dispatch is the retroactive\nreview against the committed diff.\n\nTwo consequences for how to apply the playbook below:\n\n1. The diff is at `git show HEAD` (commit 0b989cb2), not `git diff --staged`.\n   Use `git show HEAD` and `git diff HEAD~1..HEAD --name-only` instead of\n   the staged-diff commands the playbook references.\n\n2. Write your critique to `.woof/epics/E182/critique/story-S1.md` exactly as\n   the playbook specifies. Include the YAML front-matter conforming to\n   woof/schemas/critique.schema.json. Top-level severity must equal\n   max(findings[].severity). If findings is empty, omit severity (or set it\n   to null per schema).\n\nInputs to read (in addition to the playbook's input list):\n\n- .woof/.current-epic                                  \u2014 confirms E182\n- .woof/epics/E182/plan.json                           \u2014 story S1 spec\n- .woof/epics/E182/EPIC.md                             \u2014 9 outcomes, 5 CDs, 12 ACs\n- .woof/epics/E182/discovery/synthesis/PRINCIPLES.md   \u2014 P1-P6 (the operating principles the diff is meant to embody)\n- .woof/epics/E182/discovery/synthesis/ARCHITECTURE.md \u2014 registry, schemas, 9-check inventory, driver loop\n- git show HEAD                                        \u2014 the actual change under review\n- git diff HEAD~1..HEAD --name-only                    \u2014 file-level scope check vs story.paths[]\n- CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md                                \u2014 project conventions\n\nSpecific concerns flagged by the orchestrator that you should evaluate (do\nnot treat these as findings \u2014 evaluate them and report your independent\njudgement):\n\nA. Bootstrap-window deadlock risk. The registry now contains 8 placeholder\n   runners that raise NotImplementedError (checks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9 \u2014\n   only check_6_critique_blocker is real). The new wf-run driver invokes\n   `woof check stage-5 --epic --story` after the executor stages the diff,\n   and the implementation in woof/cli/commands/check.py treats every\n   NotImplementedError as `severity: blocker`. The next stories (S2 lands\n   four runners, S3 lands four more) will fail this check on every dispatch.\n   Is this captured in the diff's design comments / docstrings as a known\n   bootstrap state, or does it represent a real defect? Either answer is\n   defensible; report your finding.\n\nB. Missing story commit transaction artefacts. The S1 commit does NOT\n   include the dispatch's audit files (.woof/epics/E182/audit/cld-story-\n   executor-20260429T130650Z.{prompt,output,stderr,meta}). The new skill\n   body's step 6 says to stage .woof/epics/E<N>/audit/. Should those files\n   have been in the S1 commit?\n\nC. Self-skipped critique. The executor skipped the codex critique step\n   before committing. The orchestrator is running this retroactive review\n   to fill the gap. Is the absence of a critique-at-commit-time a finding\n   you would have raised on the diff (e.g. \"executor disabled the critique\n   path\"), or is it purely a process violation outside the diff's surface?\n\nApply the playbook below \u2014 this is the standard E182 critique contract.\n\n==============================================================================\n\n# Codex critique prompt \u2014 Stage 5 story\n\nYou are Codex, dispatched by `/wf:execute-story` to critique a single story's staged commit.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `.woof/.current-epic` \u2014 verifies the epic id `<N>`\n- `.woof/epics/E<N>/EPIC.md` \u2014 outcome + contract-decision contracts\n- `.woof/epics/E<N>/plan.json` \u2014 find the story by `story_id` (passed in the dispatch envelope)\n- `git diff --staged` (and `git diff --staged --name-only`) \u2014 the story's actual change\n- `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md` \u2014 project conventions\n\n## Output\n\nWrite `.woof/epics/E<N>/critique/story-S<k>.md` with YAML front-matter conforming to `woof/schemas/critique.schema.json` plus prose.\n\nFront-matter:\n\n```yaml\n---\nepic_id: <N>\ntarget: story\ntarget_path: .woof/epics/E<N>/plan.json\nstory_id: S<k>\ncritic: codex\nfindings:\n  - id: F1\n    severity: blocker | minor | info\n    summary: <one-line>\n    location: <file:line | story.paths[] entry>\n---\n```\n\nProse body: per finding, explain (1) what's wrong, (2) why it matters, (3) what would resolve it.\n\n## What to look for\n\n1. **Outcome fidelity.** Does the diff implement the outcome statements in `story.satisfies[]`? Are the tests *actually* verifying the outcome, or just touching the code? A test that reaches the lines but fails to assert the outcome is `blocker`.\n2. **Contract-decision implementation.** For each CD in `story.implements_contract_decisions[]`, does the diff land the implementing artefact (a route handler decorated with the OpenAPI operationId, a Pydantic class matching the ref, a JSON schema file at the declared path)? Missing implementation is `blocker`.\n3. **Scope hygiene.** Is the staged diff a subset of `story.paths[]`? (Stage 5 Check 5 also catches this deterministically; you flag the *intent* \u2014 e.g. a refactor that should have been its own story.)\n4. **Test quality.** Are tests deterministic, isolated (no shared global state, no order dependence), and asserting the right thing? Mocking against the rules in `.claude/rules/testing-database.md` is `blocker`.\n5. **Class-2 architectural concerns.** Does the diff breach BC boundaries (`import-linter` contracts), violate lazy-loading rules (`lazy=\"raise\"` on relationships), bypass auto-escaping (Jinja2 `|safe`, Astro `set:html`), use forbidden patterns (raw f-string SQL, `unittest.mock`, `allow_origins=[\"*\"]`)? All `blocker`.\n6. **Hidden coupling.** Does the diff introduce a non-obvious dependency between BCs that the plan didn't anticipate? `minor` if recoverable, `blocker` if it breaks isolation.\n\n## Severity rubric\n\n- `blocker` \u2014 the story cannot ship as-is. The 9 deterministic checks may not catch this, so spell it out.\n- `minor` \u2014 accumulates for the periodic-review valve (Stage 5 Check 9).\n- `info` \u2014 observation, no action required.\n\n## Forbidden\n\n- Don't comment on style nits the linter would already catch.\n- Don't propose alternative implementations unless the chosen one violates a `blocker` rule.\n- Don't second-guess the plan's decomposition \u2014 that's done; you're critiquing this commit only.\n- One blocker is enough to halt; enumerate the rest tersely.\n"
